<title>PORTUGAL: Banco Espirito Santo HI profit up 43 pct.</title>
<headline>Banco Espirito Santo HI profit up 43 pct.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1997-07-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months ending June 30</p>
<p>(In billions of escudos unless stated)</p>
<p>    Cons net profit	   15.22    vs    10.65</p>
<p>    Parent bank net profit  12.33    vs    10.40</p>
<p>    BIC net profit	     2.41    vs     0.93</p>
<p>    Banco Essi net profit    1.41    vs     0.31</p>
<p>    Cons banking activity   76.11    vs    58.63</p>
<p>    Operating costs	   42.17    vs    36.59</p>
<p>Note - Banco Espirito Santo is company name.  </p>
<p>    Cons net assets	3,846.00    vs 3,054.00</p>
<p>    Client loans	   1,739.00    vs 1,354.00</p>
<p>    Client deposits	2,278.00    vs 1,928.00</p>
<p>Solvability ratio (BIS definition)</p>
<p>				 13.5 pct    vs   10.6</p>
<p>Solvability ratio (Bank of Portugal definition)</p>
<p>				 11.8 pct    vs   9.3 pct</p>
<p>Cons unperforming loans</p>
<p>				  3.01 pct   vs   4.5 pct</p>
<p>Cover for unperforming</p>
<p>    loans		   107.13 pct   vs 101.94 pct</p>
<p>--Lisbon bureau 3511-3150035</p>
</text>
